  "term": "endoplasm",
  "definition": "In this historical botanical sense, endoplasm is the inner protoplasm of a plant cell that undergoes streaming movements during cyclosis. It may move back and forth along protoplasmic strands or flow in one direction within the surrounding ectoplasmic layer.",
